  "problem": "Given that $t>0,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{t}^{3})?$",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{t}^{3}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3})}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3})}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(({t}^{3})^{-1})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{3})}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{-3})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({t}^{3}-{t}^{-3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{t}^{6}-1}{{t}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{6}-1}{2{t}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
